"68.9594\"","\"28.8924\"","\"34.3341\"","\"0.7199\"","\"28.7905\"","\"dates\"","\"days\"","\"annual_sales\"","\"additional_commissioning_cash\"","\"term_year1_principal\"","\"supplier_maturity\"","\"front_operating_fraction\"","\"reported_Q1_revenue\"","\"reported_Q1_ebitda\"","\"reported_Q1_da\"","\"2026-04-30\"","\"2026-05-31\"","\"2026-06-30\"","30","31","19","\"800\"","\"0.0456\"","\"9.7177\"","\"10.9653\"","\"7.4650\"","\"9.3747\"","\"10.5147\"","\"0.5\"","\"Hypothetical cash bridge only: first three months allocated from actual Q1FY27 totals, not observed monthly cash. Remaining period uses independently assumed INR800cr annual activity pace (sensitivity700/900), not annualized one-quarter forecast. Later cash/BS ND. Original supplier maturities expire before entry. Only explicit conditional rollover replaces them. No pre-entry equity because October19 issued shares unchanged.\"","\"9.2325\"","\"bank_headroom\"","\"bank_interest\"","\"existing_interest\"","\"supplier_interest\"","\"supplier_rollover_outstanding_limit\"","\"supplier_rollover_gross_limit\"","\"supplier_tenor_months\"","\"equity_price\"","\"equity_fee\"","\"equity_gross_limit\"","\"max_new_shares\"","\"15.6658\"","\"0.11\"","\"0.095\"","\"0.105\"","\"48.80\"","\"11.1508\"","\"All additional draws, rollovers and equity are OPTIONAL UNCOMMITTED. Bank headroom revocable; gross rating quantum is not drawable cash. Whole-share equity bounded by authorized share capital and cash ceiling. No outside rescue beyond these bounds.\"","\"security\"","\"payment_month\"","\"terminal_recovery\"","\"8.20\"","\"1.46\"","\"6.74\"","\"E09\"","\"Board-approved related LLP use targeted2–3months fromSeptember2; cash payment assumedDecember19 (month2). Amount also tested pre-entry/November. No savings, return, liquidity or terminal recovery assumed without terms.\"","\"margins\"","\"receivable_ratio\"","\"inventory_ratio\"","\"other_asset_ratio\"","\"payable_ratio\"","\"advance_ratio\"","\"fixed_ratio\"","\"maintenance_ratio\"","\"deposit_ratio\"","\"receivable_loss\"","\"inventory_loss\"","\"guarantee_call\"","\"terminal_multiple\"","\"growth_driver\"","\"0.027\"","\"0.030\"","\"0.031\"","\"0.032\"","\"0.065\"","\"0.012\"","\"0.06\"","\"0.001\"","\"0.09\"","\"0.006\"","\"0.005\"","\"13.84\"","\"0.507\"","\"Volume contraction, price/mix decline, margin squeeze, delayed collections and inventory impairment occur together.\"","\"0.040\"","\"0.041\"","\"0.042\"","\"0.195\"","\"0.010\"","\"0.078\"","\"0.0013\"","\"0.085\"","\"0.0045\"","\"Certified legacy metal capacity fills gradually; no unsupported new-product sales or sudden brand pricing-power assumption. Realization stable in INR.\"","\"0.045\"","\"0.047\"","\"0.048\"","\"0.035\"","\"0.16\"","\"0.009\"","\"0.08\"","\"0.002\"","\"0.004\"","\"8\"","\"Higher value-added alloys/cables, utilization ramp and faster inventory turns. Explicit upside assumption, not current product-line revenue evidence.\"","\"Opening operating assets exclude capital advances2.3079cr and tax/financial assets; retain prepaid/supplier advances. Payables exclude capital suppliers0.1916cr. Fixed assets include CWIP, so commissioning is transfer, not duplicated capital addition.\"","\"Pre-entry four-crore incremental completion cost is uncertain, tested0/4/10; not the whole historic project cost. Maintenance additionally paid. June reported P&L not treated as observed CFO.\"","\"Contractual gross principal28.8924, separate from carrying term debt28.7905; maturity buckets9.7177,9.2817,6.2899,3.6031. Source gross debt63.2265 minus costs0.1009=63.1256 versus face63.1248, rounding0.0008 retained. No financing cost forgiven as cash. Apr–Oct fraction202/365 of year1 then balance byMarch2027; monthly approximation, not exact lender dates.\"","\"Pre-entry adjusted ONWC held initially then scales to annualsales at latest ratios. Operating generation split front/back; monthly repayment before back cash exposes intraperiod deficits.\"","\"Inventory/receivable impairment is cash replacement financing once, not both WC write-down and additional terminal haircut. No dividend or cash double count. Deposits not released to finance growth or terminal equity.\"","\"Terminal operating buffer is fixed nominal in main case, not revenue-linked cash forever. Grow-terminal-buffer sensitivity reinvests g times required operating reserve in terminalFCFF. All terminal debt settled at exit, no rescue.\"","\"method\"","\"caps\"","\"v3.0, exact Decimal, unknown means NS, no weight redistribution\"","\"5.0 due persistent CASH2 and CAP3\"","\"id\"","\"claim\"","\"used_for\"","\"A01\"","\"E01 pp73–81; E02 pp60–69\"","\"FY26 and FY25 audit opinions unmodified; CARO and IFC reviewed. Supplier finance is FY26 key audit matter. No reported fraud/default is evidence against an integrity-fail assertion, not assurance of future liquidity.\"","\"G1/GOV/G2\"","\"A02\"","\"E10 signed report/CARO/IFC\"","\"FY22 Keyur Shah opinion and IFC unmodified; Ind AS transition KAM; internal-auditor reports not considered; outgoing auditor resignation with issues considered but underlying resignation communication not located. TDS-interest dispute0.01lakh.\"","\"GOV/G2\"","\"A03\"","\"E11 signed report/CARO/IFC; E12 equivalent\"","\"FY23/24 Keyur Shah opinions and IFC unmodified. Internal audit considered; no resignation those years; FY23 TDS-interest dispute0.23lakh, FY24 none reported. FY23 group-six-CIC statement expressly management-supplied and not independently evaluated by auditor.\"","\"A04\"","\"E01 auditor appointment/directors; E02 directors\"","\"Keyur signed FY25 on28May2025 and resigned29May; Mohata Baheti appointed4June2025, formerly internal auditor. FY26 CARO says outgoing auditor raised no issues. Do not label mandatory rotation or infer concealment.\"","\"GOV/EXEC\"","\"E01 pp86–87, note19/19.1\"","\"Reported CFO8.9713 contains27.5696 supplier-finance liability increase. Reclassify as financing: CFO−18.5983. Finance-interest8.8484 is already CFF, so subtract only once for owner cash. Supplier-finance48.8343face/48.8344note.\"","\"CASH/BAL\"","\"E01 note19.1\"","\"Supplier-finance maturity buckets10.9653 within30days;7.4650 days30–60;9.3747 days60–90;21.0294 days90–150. All original balances mature before entry; later draw is new contingent finance. Finance charge4.5213.\"","\"G3/BAL\"","\"E01 notes8,9,14,16,37; E06\"","\"Available cash-and-current-account0.0822; reported equivalents0.3201 include0.2379 deposits. Total deposits3.5690 not assumed free. Headroom15.6658 terminable without notice. Debt63.1248 excludes supplier-finance48.8343.\"","\"A08\"","\"E01 note37, note38/39; E02 notes\"","\"Management indicates some debtor/creditor/advance confirmations pending; scope/value unresolved. This is not an audit qualification. Current bank balances and confirmation closures remain needed.\"","\"G2/GOV\"","\"E01 inventory and ageing notes\"","\"Inventory138.4465, including WIP134.3369. Trade receivables28.6638gross less0.1433ECL; over-six-month ageing1.2957. Metal valuation and intermediate-product scope matter.\"","\"CASH/D\"","\"E01 related-party note\"","\"Related goods sales335.5835, purchases257.6463; related receivables6.8746, payables24.6449; Zambia advance1.8931. These do not prove abuse, but group dependence and minority terms require testing.\"","\"GOV/MOAT\"","\"E09 both pages\"","\"Board approved8.20cr into new related Shera Global Ventures LLP: equity1.46 plus security contribution6.74, interest14.21%, no prior revenue, expected2–3months completion from2Sep2026. Designated partners Sheikh Naseem/Shivani. Cash payment date, redemption, savings and assured returns ND.\"","\"High approval / Low economics\"","\"GOV/G3/CAP\"","\"E01 PPE/CWIP and RPT asset sales; E02 CF\"","\"FY26 PPE+CWIP increase6.8909 plusDA3.1557 reconciles netcapex10.0466. Gross12.4701 less asset sales2.4235; RPT sales0.3535+2.07 support the latter. FY25 gross33.2045 less sale/convert15.4418 reconciles net17.7627 but gross cash/net CWIP-transfer ambiguity persists.\"","\"CAP/CASH\"","\"E03 business; E04 slide15; E01 chairman\"","\"Production FY22 4802.49MT; FY23 5093.55; FY24 6593.88; FY25 10435.69. FY26 rounded84% of13150 implies11046, not audited actual external-sale tonnes. FY24 product labels/realizations differ across documents; intermediate outputs may double count.\"","\"E01 post-year capacity discussion\"","\"Revised certified metal capacity18100MT (Al5800,Cu4300,brass5600,nickel2400), cables36000KM. Post-year revision not backdated into FY26; KM not added to tonnes. Saleable yields, mix and standalone cable revenue ND.\"","\"DUR/EXEC\"","\"E06 all six pages\"","\"FY25 volume improvement offset by cash discounts: PBILDT margin fell5.39% to3.29%. Inventory80–90days partly not order backed; commodity pass-through and fragmented competition limit pricing power. Project revised23.15 to20cr,14.91spent atMar25 and~3month delay.\"","\"MOAT/EXEC\"","\"A16\"","\"E08 full rationale/annexure\"","\"July2026 Acuite A-/A2+ upgrade uses consolidated Shera group. Group cash23.50/networth247.01 are NOT Rajputana cash/equity. Rated101.43 is NOT incremental committed credit. CARE withdrawal followed request plus lenderNOC, not recorded default.\"","\"A17\"","\"E07 March31 pattern; market masterOct19\"","\"Promoter66.08%, parentSheraEnergy51.01%; no pledge in March pattern. Later September pattern not located in available company index or exact issuer search by cutoff, so current pledge status ND. October shares22.215m confirmed independently by master.\"","\"GOV/G4\"","\"E03 objects; E02 IPO utilisation\"","\"NetIPO21.3051 used: WC14,solar4.5,general2.8051. IPO6.285m at38 plus0.6m preIPO; shares15.33m to22.215m. Authorised24.5m leaves2.285m capacity but is not an approved financing offer. No warrants/ESOP located; not proof of absence.\"","\"CAP/EARN\"","\"A19\"","\"E01 bank submissions CARO\"","\"Quarterly lender statements differ for ECL8.25/7.99/13.02/14.32lakh and inventory37.22/−20/82.37/0lakh. Reconciliation